  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "The current best is config_033 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) at 0.713 accuracy. The image-only resnet50 baseline was very weak (0.208), suggesting the image encoder may not be extracting useful features, limiting the multimodal gain (~6 pts over RNA-only). config_039 changes only the image encoder to imagenet_vit_l while keeping all other settings identical to config_033 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer, weighted fusion), cleanly isolating the image encoder effect. A stronger visual backbone could provide more complementary spatial/morphological information to the RNA modality, potentially pushing accuracy above 0.713. This is the highest-value single-variable test: if ViT helps, it confirms the image encoder was the bottleneck; if it doesn't, the RNA modality dominates and further image-side changes are low-priority. With 2 experiments remaining after this, a positive result would allow one final refinement, while a null result would confirm config_033 as the best achievable configuration."
}

